review_comments.body:
**Timer churn on every frame**: `reset()` stops the old timer and allocates a brand-new one via `time.AfterFunc` on every received frame. `time.AfterFunc` heap-allocates each time. For a high-throughput PTY session, this creates unnecessary GC pressure.

Use `time.Timer.Reset()` to reuse the existing timer instead:

```go
func (c *ptyStreamControl) arm() {
    if c.timeout <= 0 || c.disc {
        return
    }
    if c.timer == nil {
        c.timer = time.AfterFunc(c.timeout, c.onFire)
    } else {
        c.timer.Reset(c.timeout)
    }
}

func (c *ptyStreamControl) reset() {
    c.mu.Lock()
    defer c.mu.Unlock()
    if c.disc || c.fired {
        return
    }
    c.arm()
}
```

Also removes the explicit `Stop()` call since `Reset()` handles it atomically.

