review_comments.body:
🚨 **Critical: Semaphore held across retry sleeps causes head-of-line blocking**

The semaphore permit is acquired once and held for the entire retry cycle, including `tokio::time::sleep(backoff_duration(...))`. With default `max_attempts=3` and `max_backoff_secs=10`, a single failing endpoint can hold a permit for ~10.5 seconds. If 100 deliveries to a failing endpoint saturate `max_in_flight`, **all deliveries to healthy endpoints are blocked** until retries exhaust.

**Fix**: Acquire the semaphore permit per individual attempt, not once for the whole retry cycle. Release it before the backoff sleep:
```rust
// Inside the retry loop in deliver_with_retry:
for attempt in 1..=delivery.max_attempts {
    let _permit = semaphore.acquire_owned().await;  // per-attempt
    // ... send_once ...
    // _permit drops here, before sleep
    if attempt < delivery.max_attempts {
        tokio::time::sleep(backoff_duration(&delivery, attempt)).await;
    }
}
```
This ensures backoff sleep doesn't consume a semaphore slot.

