review_comments.body:
`sysconf(_SC_PAGESIZE)` returns `-1` on error (per POSIX), which when cast to `u64` becomes `0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF`. This would propagate into `MemoryRangeTable::from_bitmap` as an absurd page size, causing dirty-range arithmetic to wrap and potentially producing out-of-bounds reads during migration.

Consider validating the return value:

```rust
fn host_page_size() -> u64 {
    // SAFETY: sysconf(_SC_PAGESIZE) takes no pointer argument.
    let ret = unsafe { libc::sysconf(libc::_SC_PAGESIZE) };
    if ret <= 0 {
        let err = std::io::Error::last_os_error();
        warn!("sysconf(_SC_PAGESIZE) failed: {err}. Falling back to 4096.");
        4096
    } else {
        ret as u64
    }
}
```

The fallback to 4096 is safe because sysconf only fails on non-conforming systems and this PR already needs a dynamic value for ARM64.

