review_comments.body:
**Suggestion:** The `concurrency` option is documented as capping parallelism, but `Promise.allSettled` launches all N requests at once regardless of the requested concurrency. Consider a simple sliding-window throttle:

```ts
async function* throttle<T>(items: T[], limit: number, fn: (item: T) => Promise<Sandbox>): AsyncGenerator<Sandbox> {
  const running = new Set<Promise<Sandbox>>();
  for (const item of items) {
    while (running.size >= limit) {
      const done = await Promise.race(running);
      running.delete(done);
    }
    const p = fn(item).finally(() => running.delete(p));
    running.add(p);
    yield p;
  }
  yield* Promise.allSettled(running).then(...);
}
```

