review_comments.body:
**Potential silent failure from untrimmed annotation keys** — The parser splits on `=` but doesn't trim whitespace from the key or value. A user passing `--annotation " cube.master.vm.cgroup_v2.enable=true"` (leading space) or `--annotation "cube.master.vm.cgroup_v2.enable = true"` (spaces around `=`) will have the key silently not match the downstream constant, and the feature won't be enabled with no error or log feedback.

Consider trimming both sides before inserting into the map:
```go
key := strings.TrimSpace(kv[:idx])
val := strings.TrimSpace(kv[idx+1:])
if key == "" {
    return fmt.Errorf("invalid annotation %q: key must not be empty after trimming", kv)
}
```
The same issue applies to the value: `"true"` would become `" true"` if the user types `key= true`.

