review_comments.body:
**Docstring says "reject ... absolute paths" but implementation only checks `..`.** The function claims to reject absolute paths outside the sandbox workspace, but `"/etc/passwd"` or `"/proc/1/environ"` would pass validation. While these resolve inside the MicroVM (not the host), the documented contract is misleading.

Either update the docstring to accurately describe the function's scope, or add an absolute path check:
```python
def _sanitize_path(path: str) -> str:
    p = Path(path)
    if p.is_absolute():
        raise ValueError(f"Absolute paths not allowed: {path!r}")
    if ".." in p.parts:
        raise ValueError(f"Path traversal not allowed: {path!r}")
    return str(p)
```

